{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, sorry for the frustration. We checked your laptop (BL-LT-0106) and the main problem is that the drive is almost full: only about 3.5% of its 256 GB is free, which is why files won't save and updates fail. Please free up space with these steps: 1) Empty the Recycle Bin and clear your Downloads folder. 2) Open Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files and remove the temporary files and old Windows Update files. 3) Turn on OneDrive Files On-Demand so synced files stay in the cloud until you open them. 4) Uninstall any apps you no longer use. Then restart the laptop and reply to this ticket. If you still have less than 10% free after this, we will escalate it, since the laptop may need a larger drive or a replacement. If anything in these steps is unclear, let us know which step and we will help.",
  "internal_note": "User lookup: Leo Martins (user_id 6), Sales, Account Executive, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00. Account active, not locked, no failed logins, VPN enabled, mailbox 26% used. Device BL-LT-0106 (Windows 11 Pro), online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:45 UTC. Disk: 9.0 GB free of 256 GB (3.5%), warning 'Low disk space'. Matches KB-017 symptoms and quick check. Applied KB-017 fix steps via user guidance (cannot run cleanup remotely). Not yet re-checked after cleanup. Escalate per KB-017 if free space remains under 10% after cleanup. Ticket was vague and urgent in tone; user asked twice already, so follow up promptly. No account or security actions taken. Sign-in logs and MFA not checked since no sign-in issue reported.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
